# ─── SURA Integration ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# There is nothing to configure here anymore, and nothing to set differently
# per environment. The integration mode, the host's origin, the mini-game's
# backend UUID, and the API base URL are all decided at RUNTIME:
#
#   - mode:        "sura" whenever the game is embedded (iframe or the native
#                   app's WebView), "standalone" otherwise. Detected from
#                   window.parent / window.ReactNativeWebView — see
#                   SuraRuntimeConfig.ts.
#   - parentOrigin: captured from the origin of the host's first INIT_GAME —
#                   see SuraBridge.ts.
#   - gameId, apiBaseUrl: read from the INIT_GAME payload itself, sent by the
#                   host — see SuraIntegrationService.handleInit.
#
# One build now works in every environment (localhost, staging, production,
# and the native app, which has no fixed host origin to hardcode in the
# first place) — there's no longer a build-per-environment step.
